if you're worn out on games with drab  pallets and dramatic characters and  sunset overdrive it's just the game you  need to lift your spirits  it's a liberating experience that trades  in rules and drama for freedom and pure  unadulterated enjoyment and it never  pretends to be anything but an excuse to  swear like a sailor jump off a  skyscraper and blow up a gang of  monsters  it's the end of days after the evil  energy drink corporation Fisk Oh  poisoned almost the entire population of  Sunset city turning them into violent  rage beasts known as OD it's up to you  to kill the Horde and liberate the city  but before your crusade kicks off you  get to create a character if you're  choosing from a wide variety of silly  creative options make no mistake sunset  overdrive is immature on all fronts  nearly every character swears up a storm  dropping f-bombs like it's going out of  style  however unlike many games that take this  approach the vulgarity never feels  forced and it reinforces the attitude  that permeates the game am i right but  seriously those [ __ ] od will  tell you apart be careful  sunset city is large dense with  buildings and artifacts with plenty of  variation in architectural style  everything's coated in a bright  saturated coat of paint keeping the game  a Pixar light quality that's easy to  love when you're in the midst of battle  sometimes with what seems like 100  enemies the screen fills with explosions  bursts of lightning and bright green  ooze of course when you're zipping  across town you're going to miss a few  the finer details but you'll be having  too much fun to care one of Sunset  OverDrive's core mechanics is its  mobility system which allows you to  grind on almost everything  jump incredibly high and eventually walk  on water stringing movements together  not only gets you to your destination  safely and quickly but it really  communicates what sunset overdrive is  all about pure enjoyment sometimes you  slightly miss your mark but that's okay  because the game is very forgiving when  it comes to time once you get the hang  of each movement you can free run from  one end of the city to the other without  ever touching the ground and it's a  wonderful feeling you must explore every  nook and cranny just like you wouldn't  crackdown in order to find collectables  that go towards amps powers that boost  your abilities but you can make it  easier on yourself by purchasing maps  that pinpoint their locations as you  perform certain actions such as grinding  using automatic weapons or air dashing  you earn badges that can be traded in  for other power-ups as well sunset  overdrive is weapon options are numerous  and wild and varied enough to keep you  entertained well beyond the end of the  main mission paths you start out simply  enough with an automatic record gun in  the shotgun that sets enemies on fire  but by the end of the game you've got an  acid sprinkler a bowling ball cannon and  explosive teddy bear launcher and a gun  that bombards enemies with fireworks and  illusionary  Chinese dragons at the start it feels  like all you're doing are fetch quests  it definitely helps that moving and  shooting are so fun but you still pine  for something different after the  doesn't fetch quest in a row give it  time however and you'll discover a wider  variety of challenges including a hefty  dose of environmental traversal  challenges and combat scenarios that  keep you entertained there are also more  than a few great boss battles that  challenge your ability to act quickly  and move effectively and these are some  of the best moments in the game just me  think you're on the verge of boredom a  crazy over-the-top mission appears  reigniting your enthusiasm of course at  some point the main storyline comes to  an end and though you can freely replay  any mission in the game at a moment's  notice you should jump online and screw  around sunset city with your friends hop  into the chaos squad boots around the  map and you and a team of seven other  warriors can tackle horde like throngs  of enemies defend outposts and put your  traversal skills to the test  it is difficult with a party of less  than 8 people which may prove  problematic for some that only want to  play with a small group of friends  insomniac games is crafted an excellent  game and sunset overdrive it's not  without a few niggling issues but you'll  be too busy enjoying yourself to care  playing it makes you feel like a  super-powered kid in a candy store in a  playground you can compare it to games  like crackdown Tony Hawk's Pro Skater or  Ratchet and Clank but by combining the  best of those elements from those games  into a single package and injecting it  with an anything-goes rock and roll  attitude you never think of it as  anything but a singular achievement that  stands tall in its own merits it's  easily one of the best games on the Xbox  one and a refreshing shot of mirror
 

